# GitHub CODEOWNERS
#
# This file establishes code ownership and automatically requests reviews from designated owners
# when paths matching these patterns are changed.
#
# Usage for solo devs:
# - Leave this file empty (no active rules), or
# - Add `* @your-username` to auto-request your own review on every PR
#
# Usage for teams:
# - Add path-based rules to assign ownership domains
# - Example: `/docs/ @docs-owner` requests @docs-owner's review for docs changes
#
# Syntax:
#   <path-or-pattern> <@username> [<@username2>...]
#
# Resources:
# - https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners
#

# Example: Require docs ownership
# /docs/                                   @docs-owner

# Example: Require infrastructure ownership
# /scripts/bootstrap.sh                    @infra-owner

# Example: Solo dev auto-request
# *                                        @your-username
